                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "17dbb8aa-a455-3cc7-809f-d1aa3dc2e15f",
                        "entry_id": "7b3fdbed-78a9-3e5d-a749-4fe931c33caf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Approche critique qui va « au texte », en éliminant les attributs associés à l’auteur, au contexte de production ou, plus généralement, à l’histoire. Selon ce point de vue, l’œuvre, c’est le seul texte qui constitue le dispositif légitime pour l’exercice des activités créatrices et interprétatives."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "literary"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5bab1dd9-650d-4cc6-b773-edcf9f9fee28",
                                "sense_id": "17dbb8aa-a455-3cc7-809f-d1aa3dc2e15f",
                                "text": "Au sein de cette histoire tout neuve, trois courants principaux ce^([sic]) sont succédés, le textualisme, le contextualisme et l’actionnalisme."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "589f0017-649f-49fd-ac0b-5c5539bbdca8",
                        "source_entry_id": "7b3fdbed-78a9-3e5d-a749-4fe931c33caf",
                        "source_sense_id": "17dbb8aa-a455-3cc7-809f-d1aa3dc2e15f",
                        "target_lang_word": "textualism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "textualism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "75e06a97-764f-3068-8fbb-b284ec54880c",
                                        "entry_id": "3c80cb4d-e218-3480-bbc5-100958412a6d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Strict adherence to a text, especially to the Bible."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d86b8476-5318-419e-9659-4fcc5751eeec",
                                                "sense_id": "75e06a97-764f-3068-8fbb-b284ec54880c",
                                                "text": "First, building on the earlier work of philologists, historians, orientalists, and biblical scholars we have noted already, the late 19th and early 20th centuries witness growth and development of textualism, in which words are seen—no, revered—as the referential embodiment of meaning and truth."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "11445266-1aab-30be-bf9d-2ef1194fba81",
                                        "entry_id": "3c80cb4d-e218-3480-bbc5-100958412a6d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A formalist legal theory that interprets based on the ordinary meaning of the legal text."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe78542c-ef3f-4504-9c7d-bf934668b764",
                                                "sense_id": "11445266-1aab-30be-bf9d-2ef1194fba81",
                                                "text": "And this is the upshot of textualism: textualists do not want judges to make the law. This, at least, is the official doctrine, and it sounds very democratic."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "11f5ba96-4447-44f2-9ea2-6622c3f886c1",
                                                "sense_id": "11445266-1aab-30be-bf9d-2ef1194fba81",
                                                "text": "The Supreme Court’s conservative majority is generally committed to textualism, a judicial approach that focuses on the words of the law as written rather than its larger purpose or the intentions of its drafters. In a 2015 appearance at Harvard Law School, Justice Kagan said that textualism had triumphed across the ideological spectrum. “We’re all textualists now,” she said then."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e8a02f07-abd0-33ea-a3c2-84453bc2c3bd",
                                        "entry_id": "3c80cb4d-e218-3480-bbc5-100958412a6d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Textual criticism, especially that of the Bible."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
